    "text": "Matheus se godspellere us s\u00e6de on \u00f0ysum godspelle, \u00fe\u00e6t ure h\u00e6lend Crist, \u00f0a \u00f0a he her on life w\u00e6s on\nWite ge \u00fe\u00e6t to so\u00f0an, \u00fe\u00e6t se hiredes ealdor wacian wolde, gif he wiste \u00feone timan, hw\u00e6nne se \u00f0eof\nAnd he nolde ge\u00feafian \u00feam \u00feeofe nateshwon, \u00fe\u00e6t he underdulfe digellice his hus.\nBeo\u00f0 for \u00f0i gearwe, for\u00f0an \u00f0e ge nyton on hwylcere tide mannes sunu cume.\nHw\u00e6t wenst \u00feu la, hwa is getreowe \u00f0eow and snotor, \u00feone \u00f0e se hlaford sette ofer his hirede, \u00fee him do\nEadig bi\u00f0 se \u00f0eowa, gif he swa de\u00fe geornlice, \u00feonne se hlaford ongean cym\u00f0.\nIc cwe\u00fee to so\u00f0an, \u00fe\u00e6t he hine geset ofer ealle his god.\n\u00d0is godspell is nu ges\u00e6d sceortlice on Englisc on anfealdum gereorde, and we eac wylla\u00fe \u00fe\u00e6t andgyt\nUre h\u00e6lend \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00fe to his halgum discipulum, and \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0\u00e6t he to him cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t he cw\u00e6\u00fe eac to us:\nGe sceolon nu \u00e6rest witan, \u00fe\u00e6t twa w\u00e6ccan synd: An is \u00fe\u00e6s lichaman, o\u00f0er \u00fe\u00e6s modes.\n\u00de\u00e6s lichaman w\u00e6cce is, \u00feonne we wacia\u00f0 on cyrcan \u00e6t urum uhtsange, \u00feonne o\u00f0re men slapa\u00fe, and we\nGood is \u00fe\u00e6s lichaman w\u00e6cce, \u00fee for gode bi\u00f0 gefremod, ac \u00fe\u00e6s modes w\u00e6cce is micele betere, \u00fe\u00e6t se\nWi\u00f0standa\u00fe \u00f0am eornostlice strange on geleafan.\nLucas, se godspellere, awrat eac be \u00feysum, \u00fe\u00e6t ure h\u00e6lend s\u00e6de on sumum his godspelle be \u00f0yssere\nSeo forme w\u00e6cce is witodlice on cildhade, and seo o\u00f0er w\u00e6cce is on weaxendum cnihthade, and seo\nSe \u00f0e nolde wacian on \u00f0\u00e6re forman w\u00e6ccan, swa \u00f0\u00e6t he on cildhade gesohte his drihten and mid\nGif hwa \u00f0onne bi\u00f0, \u00fee hine sylfne forgyt on \u00feam twam w\u00e6ccum and wuna\u00f0 on his leahtrum, warnige\nUre drihten wolde, \u00fe\u00e6t us w\u00e6re bediglod se endenexta d\u00e6g \u00feises andweardan lifes, \u00fe\u00e6t we wacele\nWite ge \u00fe\u00e6t to so\u00f0an, \u00fe\u00e6t se hiredes ealdor wacian wolde, gif he wiste \u00feone timan, hw\u00e6nne se \u00f0eof\nAnd he nolde ge\u00feafian \u00feam \u00f0eofe nateshwon, \u00fe\u00e6t he underdulfe digollice his hus.\n\u00d0\u00e6s hiredes ealdor so\u00f0lice is ure agen mod, and se dyrna \u00feeof, \u00fee digollice cym\u00f0, is se gem\u00e6nelica\nGif se hiredes ealdor wende him \u00fe\u00e6s \u00f0eofes o\u00f0\u00f0e wiste his tocyme, he wolde him wi\u00f0standan, for\u00f0am\nNe m\u00e6g nan man swa \u00f0eah nahwar \u00e6tberstan \u00feam gem\u00e6nelican dea\u00f0e, \u00fee eallum mannum becym\u00f0,\nBeo\u00fe for \u00f0i gearwe, for\u00f0an \u00f0e ge nyton on hwilcere tide mannes sunu cume.\nSe h\u00e6lend us warnode mid \u00feisum wordum \u00f0us, for\u00f0an \u00f0e he wyle, \u00fe\u00e6t we ware beon, \u00fe\u00e6t we yfelum\nSe h\u00e6lend so\u00f0lice het hine sylfne mannes sunu foroft, swa swa ge gehyrdon nu, for\u00fean \u00f0e he ana is\nHw\u00e6t wenst \u00f0u la, hwa is getreowe \u00feeow and snotor, \u00feone \u00f0e se hlaford sette ofer his hirede, \u00fee him\n\u00c6lcum hlaforde gedafena\u00fe, \u00f0\u00e6t he do his mannum symle heora bigleofan on gesettum timan.\nAc se h\u00e6lend m\u00e6nde \u00feone gastlican mete, \u00fea halgan lare, \u00f0e ge men behofia\u00f0 eowrum sawlum to\nSe getreowa \u00feeowa and se snotera is se goda lareow on godes gela\u00feunge, \u00f0e seg\u00f0 \u00f0a halgan lare \u00feam\nHe d\u00e6lde wislice on gewissum timan \u00feone gastlican mete godes hirede symle, and he manega sawla\n\u00dea halgan apostolas, \u00fee \u00f0am h\u00e6lende folgodon, w\u00e6ron \u00fea getreowan \u00feeowan and \u00f0a fyrmestan\nEac heora \u00e6ftergengan and \u00f0a \u00e6\u00feelan Confessores cyddon godes lare, o\u00f0 \u00f0\u00e6t hit com to us.\nNu sceole we eac secgan \u00f0a so\u00f0an lare eow nu on urum timan, elles we beo\u00f0 gehatene yfele \u00feeowan\nSe h\u00e6lend s\u00e6de on \u00f0isum so\u00f0an godspelle: Eadig bi\u00f0 se \u00feeowa, gif he swa de\u00fe geornlice, \u00feonne se\nIc cwe\u00fee to so\u00f0an, \u00fe\u00e6t he hine geset ofer ealle his god.\nSe so\u00f0a hlaford is ure leofa h\u00e6lend.\nSe cym\u00f0 to demenne eallum mancynne, and on ure geendunge he underfeh\u00f0 us to him gif we swa\nAnd he set us ofer his god on heofonan rice on healicum wur\u00f0mynte, na \u00fe\u00e6t we ana habbon us \u00f0one\n\u00dea lareowas swinca\u00f0 swi\u00f0or \u00feonne \u00f0a l\u00e6wedan, ge on heora \u00feeowdome, \u00fee hi gode \u00feeowia\u00f0, ge on\nWe sceolon eow secgan and forsuwian ne durron, hu se \u00e6lmihtiga god foroft gewrec\u00f0 swi\u00fee his\nMoyses swustor, \u00f0\u00e6s m\u00e6ran heretogan, w\u00e6s Maria gehaten, swi\u00f0e m\u00e6re wimman.\nHeo spr\u00e6c ongean god and ongean Moysen.\nAc \u00f0\u00e6rrihte heo wear\u00f0 mid hreoflum geslagen, \u00fe\u00e6t eal hire lic egeslice tob\u00e6rst, o\u00f0 \u00f0\u00e6t Moyses eft\nOzias, se cyning, wolde eac offrian \u00e6fter Moyses \u00e6 \u00feam \u00e6lmihtigan gode \u00fea gewunelican lac.\nAc he w\u00e6s l\u00e6wede man and nam \u00fea storcyllan and sterde \u00e6t \u00feam weofode.\n\u00d0a gesloh hine sona se snawhwita hreofla, and he swa hreoflig wunode, o\u00f0 \u00f0\u00e6t he wear\u00f0 dead for\nSwi\u00f0e hra\u00f0e eac Iudas, \u00fee urne drihten bel\u00e6wde, aheng hine sylfne and swa to helle gewat.\nEac swilce Annanias, \u00fee on his agenum swicode, and his wif Saphira wurdon ofslegene \u00e6tforan \u00feam\nArrius w\u00e6s gehaten sum arleas m\u00e6ssepreost.\nSe w\u00e6s se m\u00e6sta gedwola, \u00fee wurde \u00e6fre on mancynne.\nHe wolde gelytlian urne lyfigendan drihten and wanian his godcundnysse, swa \u00fe\u00e6t he wurde\n\u00dea com him hra\u00f0e to swi\u00fee re\u00f0e wite, swa \u00fe\u00e6t him wand eal ut his inno\u00fe \u00e6t his setle, and he swa\nOlimpius hatte eac swilce an biscop.\nSe w\u00e6s eac gedwola on ures drihtnes geleafan, and he egeslice spr\u00e6c embe \u00f0a halgan \u00ferynnysse.\n\u00dea s\u00e6t he on sumum d\u00e6ge swa on his b\u00e6\u00fee, t\u00e6lende \u00feone h\u00e6lend and \u00f0a halgan \u00ferynnysse huxlice\nAc he wear\u00f0 sona eal forb\u00e6rned on \u00feam b\u00e6\u00fee middan mid gesewenlicum fyre, and ne mihte \u00fe\u00e6t b\u00e6\u00fe\nAnd his wodnys wear\u00f0 gewrecen swa \u00feurh god.\nGod wrec\u00f0 hwilon hra\u00fee, swa swa we r\u00e6ddon her, on mancynne heora mislican synna, hwilon eac\n\u00c6t fruman he behet him dea\u00fe, gif he his bebod tobr\u00e6ce.\n\u00dea tobr\u00e6c he his bebod, ac god abad swa \u00feeah nigon hund geara and \u00ferittig geara.\nAnd Adam wear\u00f0 \u00fea dead for \u00feam deopan gylte.\nCain, se bro\u00f0orslaga, \u00fee Abel ofsloh, Adames sunu, abad eac on life o\u00f0 \u00f0a seofo\u00fean m\u00e6g\u00f0e, swa swa\nAnd he sy\u00fe\u00f0an underfeng his fyrnlican d\u00e6de wite on his dea\u00fee, swa swa he wyr\u00f0e w\u00e6s.\nSaul, se cyning, \u00fee syngode ongean god and hine swa gegremode, \u00fe\u00e6t god cw\u00e6\u00fe be him, \u00fe\u00e6t him\nSalomon, se cyning, eac swilce syngode micclum ongean god and macode him deofolgyld.\nAc for his f\u00e6der geearnungum, \u00fe\u00e6s \u00e6\u00f0elan Davides, god him let fyrst feowertig geara, and his\n\u00d0a Iudeiscan syngodon swi\u00f0e ongean god, \u00fea \u00fea hi acwealdon Crist, urne h\u00e6lend.\nAc god him let fyrst swa \u00feeah feowertig geara, \u00fe\u00e6t hi heora synna sceoldon behreowsian.\nAc \u00f0a \u00fea hi ne dydon nane d\u00e6dbote, \u00fea sende him god to \u00feone scearpan here Romaniscre leode, \u00fee\nFela we mihton secgan swilcera bysena, gif hit to langsum n\u00e6re on \u00feysum lytlan cwyde.\nAc we secga\u00fe swa \u00feeah: Se \u00f0e his scyppend grema\u00fe, \u00fe\u00e6t hit bi\u00f0 gewrecen gewislice on him, swa \u00e6r,\nGod gewrec\u00f0 his forsewennysse, swa swa we s\u00e6don \u00e6r, hwilon \u00e6r, hwilon lator, locahu him gewyr\u00f0.\nHwilon he gewitna\u00fe \u00f0\u00e6s mannes gewitleaste sona mid styrnysse, o\u00f0rum to steore and eac \u00fe\u00e6t he to\nHwilon he andbida\u00f0, swa swa we \u00e6r cw\u00e6don, for his micclan ge\u00feylde, \u00fe\u00e6t se man gecyrre fram his\nFor \u00f0i synd witan gesette and wise lareowas, \u00fe\u00e6t hi sceolon styran stuntra manna anginne, \u00fe\u00e6t, gif se\n\u00c6lc \u00f0ing sceal habban sumne ege on his life, ge fur\u00f0on \u00fea wildan deor, \u00fee on wuda eardia\u00fe.\nWe r\u00e6da\u00fe be \u00fe\u00e6re leon, \u00f0e is swa re\u00f0e deor, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0urh hyre grymetunge, \u00feonne heo gr\u00e6dig bi\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0a\nAc swa \u00feeah seo leo \u00feone lytlan hanan hyre ondr\u00e6t, gif heo him on besyh\u00f0, and ealra swi\u00f0ost, gif se\nEac se micela ylp, \u00fee \u00f0a modigan fearras mid ealle ofbeat mid his egeslican nypele, ondr\u00e6t him\nNu habba\u00f0 deor ege him betwynan, and \u00fea wildan deor be ures drihtnes gesetnysse syndon mannum\nAmen.",
